{
  "description": "A tier name that cannot be a rulebook filename. Custom tiers are first-class, so the doctor does not police the tier's MEANING — only that the name can address a file. The underscore is what is refused here. It is NOT 'Backend', which this fixture tried first and which the doctor ACCEPTS — PowerShell's -notmatch is case-insensitive, so the regex does not enforce the lowercase its own message promises, and on a case-sensitive filesystem the SAME record then fails the next rule instead. Recorded as a finding (notes.md, T031) rather than enshrined: the fix is -cnotmatch, and scripts/ are outside phase 4's territory.",
